 "notes": "The source side. can counts with may because every target language renders both with one word. Kinds are compared in order, so must then may is not may then must. Negation is read within three words before and one after a modal (does not require is need-not). one is not a number word: it is too often a pronoun. Digits stay digits in a translation: one hour against 1 hora blocks.",
